  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 131 PM EDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\n- Severe Thunderstorm Risk This Afternoon\n\nA Severe Thunderstorm Watch is in effect until 8PM this Evening.\nThe areas of interest are the storms that will move in from\nWisconsin and over Lake Michigan into the area. Additional\ndevelopment ahead of the line is possible with remnant boundaries\nin the current unstable high shear environment. The highest threat\nfor severe thunderstorms will be along and west of US-131 with\nlower confidence further east as instability decreases.\n\nAll hazards will be in play with effective shear values around 50\nknots, ML CAPE values increasing to 3000 J/kg, and 0-3km SRH\nvalues around 100 to 200 m2/s2. Overall guidance hasn't had a\ngreat grasp on thunderstorm development and evolution. We are in a\nhigh risk low confidence situation. If storms are widespread \nthrough this afternoon and clear this evening, the rest of the \nnight should be largely dry. If the environment isn't worked over \nwe could see additional development overnight.\n\n- Rain and Thunderstorm Chances Return Friday into the Weekend\n\nAs the shortwave responsible for today's thunderstorms moves east,\npressure heights increase with dry conditions expected through\nmost of the week. Temperatures will largely be in the 80s each day\nwith lows in the 50s and 60s. Rain and thunderstorm chances \nincrease Friday into Saturday with another trough. Chances may \nlinger into Sunday depending on how fast the trough clears the \narea.",
